WEBVTT

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:08.720
And now it is my privilege and honor to introduce Robert Kennedy.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:28.560
On a hot August night in 1964, Robert F. Kennedy mounted the podium at the Democratic Convention in Atlantic City.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:40.230
It was first a rumble and then a roar and pretty soon it just consumed the whole place and they would not stop.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:50.790
They simply would not stop. I don't know, 15, 16, 17, 18 minutes, I don't remember how long it was.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.350
I only remember that I couldn't stop crying.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:59.980
It didn't surprise me that they would not stop.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.440
not let him speak, not let go of him.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:09.460
He was the representation of what they had lost.

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:16.410
And if the delegates had a sense of loss,

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:19.000
imagine what his feelings were.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.120
Every day, every hour, every minute,

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:24.560
he felt the loss of his brother.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.690
10 months before, President John Kennedy

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:40.340
assassinated in dallas bobby had given his life to his brother as confidant protector lightning rod

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:52.490
now his brother was gone and he was left to carry on alone he was not really built for the spotlight

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:59.380
he was built for the wings he had a fight against a basic shiners a basic

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:07.680
in public. Many times I would stand behind the stage and I would see his legs shaking

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:16.690
during a speech or his hands shaking. He wasn't a natural, but that all had to change when

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:23.370
his brother was assassinated. And I think change is the motif of his whole life and

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:29.740
career. He really becomes something much larger than what he was when he began.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.820
He becomes stronger through suffering.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:40.900
The pandemonium went on for 22 long minutes.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:47.940
As the crowd grew quiet, he bared his grief,

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.000
enshrining his brother in words from Romeo and Juliet.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:58.160
I think of President Kennedy, I think of...

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:05.250
But Shakespeare said in Romeo and Juliet that when he shall die,

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.300
take him and cut him out in little stars,

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.660
and he shall make the face of heaven so fine

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:14.600
that all the world will be in love with night,

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.810
paying no worship to the garish sun.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:37.280
When he was finished speaking, he left the hall, sat on a fire escape, and wept.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:59.980
In the spring of 19...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.720
1952, Massachusetts Congressman John Kennedy was keeping up a brave face

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:10.410
while his campaign for the United States Senate unraveled into chaos.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:15.360
He desperately needed a tough, disciplined campaign manager.

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:20.830
As he would for the rest of his life, he reached out to his kid brother.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.480
Bobby didn't want to do it.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:28.000
He already had a job, working as a lawyer in the Justice Department.

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:29.970
But Robert...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.780
Robert F. Kennedy knew what his family expected.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:37.590
For the next 12 years, he would devote himself to Jack,

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.740
putting his brother's ambitions before his own.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:44.650
That had been the great lesson of his childhood.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:52.030
As the third boy and the seventh of nine children,

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.840
Bobby Kennedy easily got lost.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:59.960
He was born in Brookline, Massachusetts, on November 12th.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:05.960
20th, 1925. All through his early years, he struggled just to keep up.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:23.080
Everything was a competition, within the family and without. They still talk, this little

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:28.500
yacht club in Hyannis, about how the Kennedys cheated by adding more sailcloth to their boats.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:33.460
The Kennedys were very competitive, and they wanted to win at everything they did.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:40.400
We don't want any losers around here, Joseph Kennedy told all his children.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.980
In this family, we want winners.

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:48.260
Don't come in second or third. That doesn't count. Win.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:54.140
Bobby's father was the towering figure in his childhood.

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:59.920
Joseph P. Kennedy had made millions with shrewd investments in the stock market.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.520
the movies, and, some say, by bootlegging liquor.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:06.580
But he wanted more out of life than money.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:10.800
He wanted his two oldest sons, Joe Jr. and Jack,

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:12.750
to win elected office.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:18.400
And even more, he wanted Joe Jr. to become president someday.

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:21.610
This would give the family a kind of visibility,

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:25.030
a kind of cachet, a kind of social status

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:27.410
that Joe Kennedy was very hungry for.

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:29.970
And the children imbibed this.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:38.900
ambition. While Joe's attention was lavished on his two oldest boys, Bobby quietly took his place

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:49.480
among the younger children, the girls. He was small, awkward, shy. His father described him as

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:59.000
the family runt. He would set out to prove he was as tough as his brothers. When he was only four,

00:06:59.180 --> 00:06:59.980
he dove off the...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:06.200
family sailboat in a desperate attempt to prove he could swim ashore. As he was going under, Joe

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:14.020
Jr. had to haul him out. It either showed a lot of guts, Jack said later, or no sense at all. And

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:19.920
that's how Bobby got his father's attention, by being the tough guy. But beneath that toughness,

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:28.550
there was always the softness and the sensitivity. He was a mama's boy. In fact, his grandmother

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:29.650
worried that he was...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:34.540
Too much of a sissy, too much of a girly boy, because he clung to his mother's skirts.

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:41.210
Rose Kennedy was a devout Catholic, and Bobby absorbed her religious intensity.

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:47.920
He made his first communion when he was seven, and went on to become an altar boy,

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:51.020
and attend a school run by Benedictine monks.

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:59.970
Bobby Kennedy grew up with a strong sense of right and wrong, good and evil, like his brother.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:00.260
others.

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:03.250
he was toughened by the rigorous demands of his father.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:06.790
but he disguised as well a gentler nature.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:09.640
Bobby, a friend said.

00:08:10.230 --> 00:08:12.250
was truly in touch with his emotions.

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:14.530
He was saved.

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:15.480
by being.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:16.340
overlooked.

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:23.260
When World War II began,

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:25.080
Bobby was in high school.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:28.410
and chafed to get into the action, like his two older brothers.

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:32.820
He flushed with pride when Jack became a hero.

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:38.810
rescuing most of his crew after his PT boat was sliced in two by a Japanese destroyer.

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:40.610
but disaster.

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:41.810
was to follow.

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:44.810
and determine the direction of Bobby's life.

00:08:45.070 --> 00:08:46.050
Thank you.

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:49.190
in the summer of 1944.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:53.380
Joe Jr. volunteered for a near-suicidal mission.

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:56.820
to pilot a plane loaded with dynamite.

00:08:57.190 --> 00:08:58.270
toward an enemy target.

00:08:59.270 --> 00:08:59.970
And then perish.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:00.800
shoot to safety.

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:04.140
His plane exploded.

00:09:04.630 --> 00:09:05.810
before he ever got there.

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:06.820
You

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:10.200
Joe Jr. was dead.

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:14.310
along with all the hopes his father had invested in him.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:17.980
Now it would be up to Jack.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:20.080
to realize his father's ambitions.

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:22.640
And it would become Bobby's role.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:23.680
to help him.

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:26.970
But Bobby was young.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:28.300
Only 18.

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:29.990
Still struggling.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.060
to determine his own destiny.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:33.920
Thank you.

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:37.780
In 1948,

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:39.800
He graduated from Harvard.

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:43.120
went on to law school.

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:44.820
Thank you.

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:48.850
and then became the first of the Kennedy boys to settle down.

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:52.880
24 years old.

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:54.760
He married Ethel Skakel.

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:56.100
Wealthy.

00:09:56.330 --> 00:09:56.950
Outgoing.

00:09:57.350 --> 00:09:58.090
Athletic.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:09:59.940
So do.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:00.320
out.

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:02.070
She had almost become a nun.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:08.460
A year later.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:11.300
The first of his 11 children was born.

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:14.970
When it came to those he loved,

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:16.590
Bobby was tender.

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:17.730
Maternal.

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:21.940
but he turned a hardened face to the world.

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:29.960
He was particularly edgy and volatile, and I think unhappy when he was in.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.000
his early 20s.

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:33.100
He was an angry young man.

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:34.780
I mean, he was always getting into fistfights.

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:37.940
I mean, his temper was about that far from the surface.

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:43.780
In 1952, when he managed his brother's victorious run for the Senate,

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:46.800
Robert Kennedy gained a reputation as

00:10:47.050 --> 00:10:47.730
Ruthless.

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:49.220
A rude...

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:50.870
arrogant, impatient kid.

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:53.590
But he shrugged off complaints.

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:56.880
I don't care if anyone around here likes me.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:57.730
Bobby said.

00:10:58.340 --> 00:10:59.780
as long as they like Jack.

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:06.190
Now with Jack in the Senate, Bobby would darken his reputation further

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:09.560
when his father got him a job with a family friend,

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:12.730
one of the most controversial men in America,

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:14.870
Wisconsin Senator...

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:22.550
Joseph McCarthy. Any man who has been given the honor of being promoted to general and who says

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:28.850
I will protect another general who protects communists is not fit to wear that uniform,

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:29.450
general.

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:31.940
In 1953,

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:36.660
Bobby enlisted in McCarthy's crusade against what both men saw.

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:39.310
as the evil of communism in America.

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:43.500
Robert Kennedy in the 1950s was very much his father's son.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:45.800
His father was fiercely anti-communist.

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:48.240
Joe Kennedy saw it.

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:51.270
Joe McCarthy is doing the Lord's work.

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:54.900
History thinks of Joe McCarthy as this virulent red baiter.

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:59.510
But Bobby Kennedy was a black and white moralist at this stage of his life.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:05.220
And the communists were the bad guys, and anybody who was against the communists was...

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:11.250
therefore a good guy, and so he liked the kind of black and white morality that Joe McCarthy was selling.

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:16.730
What was striking about Bobby was not that he worked for Joe McCarthy so much,

00:12:16.950 --> 00:12:19.790
but rather that he admired Joe McCarthy.

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:22.710
and became very close to Joe McCarthy.

00:12:23.540 --> 00:12:23.920
So,

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:29.590
when McCarthy was conducting his investigations into suspected communists.

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:32.940
but I'd be enthusiastically joined in this role.

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:36.480
Bobby worked for McCarthy for six months.

00:12:36.970 --> 00:12:37.890
then moved on.

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:41.780
still grimly determined to root out evil in America.

00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:48.040
I decline to answer this question on the grounds that the answer may tend to incriminate.

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:50.480
The decline of the ants on the ground.

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:54.760
The answer, I'll be grimly attend, I'll be grimly myself.

00:12:55.820 --> 00:12:59.800
Somebody that's been as successful as you can remember how to say I declined to answer.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:02.030
So don't put that act on.

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:03.170
I want to mature.

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:06.690
As chief legal counsel for what became known

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:08.150
as the Senate Rackets Committee,

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:11.780
Bobby began probing into labor unions and mobsters.

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:14.920
grilling some of the toughest gangsters in America.

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:20.010
But no one rankled him more than Jimmy Hoffa.

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:23.590
Hoffa was president of the Brotherhood of Teamsters.

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:25.070
the country's largest...

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:25.820
richest

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:28.300
and one of its most corrupt unions.

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:29.960
Bobby said he.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.140
detected in Hoffa.

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:33.000
Absolute evilness.

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:34.010
Thank you very much.

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:36.320
...say anything to the fact that the jury...

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:37.660
treated you very well.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:40.580
and that you thought that you could do very well before a jury.

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:42.020
You know, that's pretty ridiculous.

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:43.400
Did you say anything like that?

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:43.860
I did not.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:45.460
And I appeal to the chair.

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:47.500
Let that be taken out of the record.

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:53.560
Bobby turned his investigation of Hoffa into a holy cause.

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:56.200
holding hearings month after month.

00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:59.540
and calling more than 1,500 witnesses.

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:03.020
Punishing Hoffa.

00:14:03.220 --> 00:14:04.640
became a crusade.

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:05.800
Detroit.

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:08.520
At least 15 who have police records.

00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:10.890
You've got Joey Glimco in Chicago.

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:14.020
I say you're not tough enough to get rid of these people then.

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:16.550
But Hoffa was contemptuous.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:18.600
He denied any wrongdoing.

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:21.070
taunting the crusading young investigator.

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:22.700
Did you say...

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:25.040
That SOB, I'll break his back.

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:25.700
Who?

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:26.530
You.

00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:27.810
Thank the who?

00:14:28.280 --> 00:14:28.880
to anyone.

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:29.960
Figurist speech.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.520
I don't even know who I was talking about, and I don't know what you're talking about.

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:36.210
Well, Mr. Hoffman, all I'm trying to find out, I'll tell you what I'm talking about.

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:37.070
I'm trying to find out.

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:38.650
whose back you are going to break.

00:14:39.180 --> 00:14:40.160
Thank you for your speech.

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:42.330
Thank you for your speech.

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:44.770
I used to love, Hoffa said.

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:46.470
to bug the little bastard.

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:50.280
Bobby could never bring Hoffa down.

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:51.970
But his zealous efforts

00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:54.410
won him the attention of the nation's press.

00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:56.820
much to the delight of his brother Jack.

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:59.550
who was a member of the Senate Rackets Committee, too.

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:00.560
You

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:05.950
Two boyish young men from Boston, wrote a reporter in Look magazine.

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:09.030
have become hot tourist attractions in Washington.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:21.460
The Kennedys' fabulous wealth.

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:23.030
their marriages,

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:24.200
They're glamour.

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:27.420
all made them favorites of the picture magazines.

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:34.470
I think he found himself during the Hoffa investigation, a friend said.

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:36.740
For the first time in his life,

00:15:37.420 --> 00:15:38.480
Bobby was happy.

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:39.900
Thank you.

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:40.580
Thank you.

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:43.510
But in September 1959,

00:15:44.390 --> 00:15:48.110
Bobby resigned from the Senate Rackets Committee, where he had made his mark.

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:50.940
His brother was running for president.

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:52.560
Thank you.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:02.520
When Jack set out to win the Democratic nomination,

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:05.960
Bobby once again put his own ambitions aside.

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:10.630
He would do whatever it took to get his brother elected.

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:15.630
While Jack rose above the fray,

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:19.680
Bobby took on the gritty day-to-day business of running the campaign.

00:16:20.760 --> 00:16:22.440
pushing his staffers to their limits.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.020
Jack's opponents.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.500
becoming the campaign's dark driving force.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:35.600
As one journalist put it,

00:16:36.330 --> 00:16:38.830
Whenever you see Bobby Kennedy in public with his brother,

00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:41.740
He looks as though he showed up for a rumble.

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:52.370
By the time the Democrats met for their convention in Los Angeles,

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:55.550
Kennedy seemed to have the nomination wrapped up.

00:16:56.260 --> 00:16:59.780
But Lyndon Johnson, the powerful Senate Majority Leader from Texas,

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:01.580
set out to stop him.

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:03.560
The person you select is your friend.

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:05.880
Here's judgment.

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:10.390
Responsibilities he's shouldered, the weight he's carrying.

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:11.980
The burdens he knows.

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:16.490
The decision he makes may well determine whether...

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:17.420
You love us.

00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:18.380
Three men.

00:17:20.860 --> 00:17:24.480
LBJ was one of America's smartest political operators.

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:27.040
But Bobby outmaneuvered him.

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:29.640
skillfully working the convention floor.

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:32.920
making sure that LBJ didn't get the votes.

00:17:35.300 --> 00:17:36.280
We'll see you next time.

